  "metricScope": "RGB8 mean absolute difference on common foreground in lower image half (y>=480), not a physical lighting measure. Source PNGs before/after are pixel-identical.",
  "findings": [
    "Root reviewed both corrected contact sheets. Bright inner/lower-robe mismatch substantially resolves toward the skeletal reference on both variants.",
    "At unchanged positions/material settings, replacing only four sampled normal frames improves lower-robe rendering. Coarse folds/hem and trim differences remain; Elder mantle fold shading is still visibly different.",
    "Reference conversion normals match exactly, but posed baked normals differ by up to146.87 degrees Elder and176.74 degrees Woman. Corresponding position differences stay below0.281cm. This isolates animated normal transfer as a contributor.",
    "Corrected PNGs retain every unselected texel and alpha byte. They are partial diagnostic textures, imported without saving and bound only to transient MIDs. Never adopt these four-frame files into runtime."
  ],
  "next": "Bake direct skeletal normals for complete walk and idle clips into a fresh candidate, then multi-view/transition review. Continue body reduction, all-cast and thousands-of-people runtime testing.",
